-- Source: de-code-t8-ch1-2026-10-01.txt, a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from the
-- Delaware Code Online (through 85 Del. Laws, c. 550). It is not the official text. `-- src:N | ...` is
-- line N of that file (an ellipsis means the line goes on).
--
-- Layer 1 takes nobody's point of view: each rule is the relation the text states between the corporation, its
-- creditors and stockholders, a receiver or trustee and the Court of Chancery. What the Court "may" do, or "deems"
-- or "directs", is a plain input and is never guessed. Whether a corporation "shall be insolvent" is a fact the
-- caller states; the Law gives no test of insolvency in this range.
-- Out of range, taken as plain inputs: section 102(b)(2) (piece dg1), section 103 (piece dg1), section 391 (piece dg11),
-- the Rules of the Court of Chancery and the Federal Bankruptcy Code, 11 U.S.C. § 101 et seq. (neither among the inputs).

§ `Subchapter XI. Insolvency; Receivers and Trustees`

§§ `s 291 Receivers for insolvent corporations; appointment and powers`

-- "Whenever a corporation shall be insolvent, the Court of Chancery, on the application of any creditor or
-- stockholder thereof, may, at any time, appoint 1 or more persons to be receivers of and for the corporation".
-- The applicant is a party of the core's cast. The Court "may": the rule says only that the text puts the Court in a
-- position to act on this application; it never says the Court will.
-- src:1523 | Whenever a corporation shall be insolvent, the Court of Chancery, on the application of any creditor or stockholder thereof, may, at any time, appoint 1 or more persons to be receivers of and for the corporation, to take charge of its assets, estate, effects, business and affairs, and to collect the outstanding debts, claims, and property due and belonging to the corporation, with power to prosecute and defend, in the name of the corporation or otherwise, all claims or suits, to appoint an agent or agents under them, and to do all other acts which might be done by the corporation and which may be necessary or proper. The powers of the receivers shall be such and shall continue so long as the Court shall deem necessary.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 291 (src:1523)
GIVEN `the corporation is insolvent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant` IS AN Actor
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 291 the Court of Chancery may act on the application to appoint receivers for the insolvent corporation` MEANS
        `the corporation is insolvent`
    AND (CONSIDER `the applicant`
         WHEN `a creditor` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `a stockholder` THEN TRUE
         OTHERWISE FALSE)

-- src:1523 | to take charge of its assets, estate, effects, business and affairs, and to collect the outstanding debts, claims, and property due and belonging to the corporation, with power to prosecute and defend, in the name of the corporation or otherwise, all claims or suits, to appoint an agent or agents under them, and to do all other acts which might be done by the corporation and which may be necessary or proper. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 291 (src:1523)
DECLARE `s 291 Power of a receiver` IS ONE OF
    `to take charge of the assets, estate, effects, business and affairs of the corporation`
    `to collect the outstanding debts, claims, and property due and belonging to the corporation`
    `to prosecute and defend, in the name of the corporation or otherwise, all claims or suits`
    `to appoint an agent or agents under the receivers`
    `to do all other acts which might be done by the corporation and which may be necessary or proper`

-- src:1523 | to take charge of its assets, estate, effects, business and affairs, and to collect the outstanding debts, claims, and property due and belonging to the corporation, with power to prosecute and defend, in the name of the corporation or otherwise, all claims or suits, to appoint an agent or agents under them, and to do all other acts which might be done by the corporation and which may be necessary or proper. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 291 (src:1523)
`s 291 the powers of the receivers` MEANS
    LIST `to take charge of the assets, estate, effects, business and affairs of the corporation`
       , `to collect the outstanding debts, claims, and property due and belonging to the corporation`
       , `to prosecute and defend, in the name of the corporation or otherwise, all claims or suits`
       , `to appoint an agent or agents under the receivers`
       , `to do all other acts which might be done by the corporation and which may be necessary or proper`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 291 (src:1523)
GIVEN `the power` IS A `s 291 Power of a receiver`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 291 the receivers have the power` MEANS
    elem `the power` `s 291 the powers of the receivers`

-- "The powers of the receivers shall be such and shall continue so long as the Court shall deem necessary."
-- src:1523 | The powers of the receivers shall be such and shall continue so long as the Court shall deem necessary.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 291 (src:1523)
GIVEN `the Court of Chancery deems the continuation of the powers necessary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 291 the powers of the receivers continue` MEANS
    `the Court of Chancery deems the continuation of the powers necessary`

§§ `s 292 Title to property; filing order of appointment; exception`

-- Subsection (a): trustees or receivers appointed by the Court of Chancery "shall, upon their appointment and
-- qualification or upon the death, resignation or discharge of any co-trustee or co-receiver, be vested by operation of
-- law and without any act or deed, with the title of the corporation to all of its property, real, personal or mixed ...
-- except real estate situate outside this State." Subsection (c): the section does not apply to receivers appointed
-- pendente lite.
-- src:1527 | (a) Trustees or receivers appointed by the Court of Chancery of and for any corporation, and their respective survivors and successors, shall, upon their appointment and qualification or upon the death, resignation or discharge of any co-trustee or co-receiver, be vested by operation of law and without any act or deed, with the title of the corporation to all of its property, real, personal or mixed of whatsoever nature, kind, class or description, and wheresoever situate, except real estate situate outside this State.
-- src:1529 | (c) This section shall not apply to receivers appointed pendente lite.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 292(a) (src:1527), (c) (src:1529)
GIVEN `the trustees or receivers were appointed by the Court of Chancery` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the trustees or receivers are receivers appointed pendente lite` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the trustees or receivers have been appointed and have qualified, or a co-trustee or co-receiver has died, resigned or been discharged` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the property is real estate situate outside this State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 292(a) title of the corporation to the property is vested in the trustees or receivers by operation of law` MEANS
        `the trustees or receivers were appointed by the Court of Chancery`
    AND (NOT `the trustees or receivers are receivers appointed pendente lite`)
    AND `the trustees or receivers have been appointed and have qualified, or a co-trustee or co-receiver has died, resigned or been discharged`
    AND (NOT `the property is real estate situate outside this State`)

-- Subsection (b): they "shall, within 20 days from the date of their qualification, file in the office of the recorder in
-- each county in this State, in which any real estate belonging to the corporation may be situated, a certified copy of
-- the order of their appointment and evidence of their qualification". A filing on the 20th day is within the 20 days.
-- src:1528 | (b) Trustees or receivers appointed by the Court of Chancery shall, within 20 days from the date of their qualification, file in the office of the recorder in each county in this State, in which any real estate belonging to the corporation may be situated, a certified copy of the order of their appointment and evidence of their qualification.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 292(b) (src:1528)
`s 292(b) the time after qualification to file in the office of the recorder` MEANS `period in days` 20

@ref 8 Del. C. § 292(b) (src:1528)
GIVEN `the trustees or receivers were appointed by the Court of Chancery` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the trustees or receivers are receivers appointed pendente lite` IS A BOOLEAN
      `real estate belonging to the corporation is situated in the county` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 292(b) the trustees or receivers must file a certified copy of the order of appointment and evidence of qualification in the office of the recorder of the county` MEANS
        `the trustees or receivers were appointed by the Court of Chancery`
    AND (NOT `the trustees or receivers are receivers appointed pendente lite`)
    AND `real estate belonging to the corporation is situated in the county`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 292(b) (src:1528)
GIVEN `the date of their qualification` IS A DATE
      `the date they filed in the office of the recorder of the county, if they did` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 292(b) the filing in the office of the recorder was made in time` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date they filed in the office of the recorder of the county, if they did`
    WHEN JUST filed THEN filed AT MOST (`the date` `s 292(b) the time after qualification to file in the office of the recorder` `after` `the date of their qualification`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE

§§ `s 293 Notices to stockholders and creditors`

-- "All notices required to be given to stockholders and creditors in any action in which a receiver or trustee for a
-- corporation was appointed shall be given by the Register in Chancery, unless otherwise ordered by the Court of Chancery."
-- src:1533 | All notices required to be given to stockholders and creditors in any action in which a receiver or trustee for a corporation was appointed shall be given by the Register in Chancery, unless otherwise ordered by the Court of Chancery.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 293 (src:1533)
GIVEN `a notice is required to be given to stockholders and creditors in an action in which a receiver or trustee for the corporation was appointed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court of Chancery has ordered that the notice be given otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 293 the notice is to be given by the Register in Chancery` MEANS
        `a notice is required to be given to stockholders and creditors in an action in which a receiver or trustee for the corporation was appointed`
    AND (NOT `the Court of Chancery has ordered that the notice be given otherwise`)

§§ `s 294 Receivers or trustees; inventory; list of debts and report`

-- "Trustees or receivers shall, as soon as convenient, file in the office of the Register in Chancery of the county in
-- which the proceeding is pending, a full and complete itemized inventory of all the assets of the corporation which
-- shall show their nature and probable value, and an account of all debts due from and to it, as nearly as the same can
-- be ascertained." The text fixes no number of days ("as soon as convenient"), so no date rule is written (fork F10).
-- src:1537 | Trustees or receivers shall, as soon as convenient, file in the office of the Register in Chancery of the county in which the proceeding is pending, a full and complete itemized inventory of all the assets of the corporation which shall show their nature and probable value, and an account of all debts due from and to it, as nearly as the same can be ascertained. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 294 (src:1537)
