§§ `s 295 Creditors’ proofs of claims; when barred; notice`

-- "All creditors shall make proof under oath of their respective claims against the corporation, and cause the same to
-- be filed in the office of the Register in Chancery of the county in which the proceeding is pending within the time
-- fixed by and in accordance with the procedure established by the rules of the Court of Chancery." The time fixed is the
-- Court's (rules or order; not among the inputs), so the last day is a plain input.
-- src:1541 | All creditors shall make proof under oath of their respective claims against the corporation, and cause the same to be filed in the office of the Register in Chancery of the county in which the proceeding is pending within the time fixed by and in accordance with the procedure established by the rules of the Court of Chancery. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 295 (src:1541)
GIVEN `the creditor made proof of the claim under oath` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the creditor caused the proof to be filed in the office of the Register in Chancery of the county in which the proceeding is pending` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the proof was filed` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the last day fixed for filing proofs of claim by the rules of the Court of Chancery or the order of the Court` IS A DATE -- out of range: the rules of the Court of Chancery are not among the inputs
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 295 the creditor has made and filed proof of the claim as the section requires` MEANS
        `the creditor made proof of the claim under oath`
    AND `the creditor caused the proof to be filed in the office of the Register in Chancery of the county in which the proceeding is pending`
    AND (CONSIDER `the date the proof was filed`
         WHEN JUST filed THEN filed AT MOST `the last day fixed for filing proofs of claim by the rules of the Court of Chancery or the order of the Court`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE)

-- "All creditors and claimants failing to do so, within the time limited by this section, or the time prescribed by the
-- order of the Court, may, by direction of the Court, be barred from participating in the distribution of the assets of
-- the corporation." The bar comes only by the Court's direction: a creditor who failed and has not been so directed is
-- not yet barred and not yet safe, so that case answers NOTHING.
-- src:1541 | All creditors and claimants failing to do so, within the time limited by this section, or the time prescribed by the order of the Court, may, by direction of the Court, be barred from participating in the distribution of the assets of the corporation. The Court may also prescribe what notice, by publication or otherwise, shall be given to the creditors of the time fixed for the filing and making proof of claims.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 295 (src:1541)
GIVEN `the creditor has made and filed proof of the claim as section 295 requires` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court of Chancery has directed that the creditor be barred from participating in the distribution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 295 the creditor is barred from participating in the distribution of the assets` MEANS
    IF `the creditor has made and filed proof of the claim as section 295 requires`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE (IF `the Court of Chancery has directed that the creditor be barred from participating in the distribution` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING)

-- "The Court may also prescribe what notice, by publication or otherwise, shall be given to the creditors of the time
-- fixed for the filing and making proof of claims."
-- src:1541 | The Court may also prescribe what notice, by publication or otherwise, shall be given to the creditors of the time fixed for the filing and making proof of claims.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 295 (src:1541)
GIVEN `the Court of Chancery has prescribed what notice, by publication or otherwise, is to be given to the creditors of the time fixed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the prescribed notice has been given to the creditors` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 295 the creditors have been given the notice the Court of Chancery prescribed` MEANS
    (NOT `the Court of Chancery has prescribed what notice, by publication or otherwise, is to be given to the creditors of the time fixed`) OR `the prescribed notice has been given to the creditors`

§§ `s 296 Adjudication of claims; appeal`

-- Subsection (a): the Register in Chancery notifies the trustee or receiver immediately upon the expiration of the time
-- fixed for filing claims; "the trustee or receiver, within 30 days after receiving the notice, shall inspect the claims".
-- src:1545 | The Register in Chancery, immediately upon the expiration of the time fixed for the filing of claims, in compliance with § 295 of this title, shall notify the trustee or receiver of the filing of the claims, and the trustee or receiver, within 30 days after receiving the notice, shall inspect the claims, and if the trustee or receiver or any creditor shall not be satisfied with the validity or correctness of the same, or any of them, the trustee or receiver shall forthwith notify the creditors whose claims are disputed of such trustee’s or receiver’s decision. The trustee or receiver shall require all creditors whose claims are disputed to submit themselves to such examination in relation to their claims as the trustee or receiver shall direct, and the creditors shall produce such books and papers relating to their claims as shall be required. The trustee or receiver shall have power to examine, under oath or affirmation, all witnesses produced before such trustee or receiver touching the claims, and shall pass upon and allow or disallow the claims, or any part thereof, and notify the claimants of such trustee’s or receiver’s determination.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 296(a) (src:1545)
`s 296(a) the time after the notice to inspect the claims` MEANS `period in days` 30

@ref 8 Del. C. § 296(a) (src:1545)
GIVEN `the date the trustee or receiver received the Register's notice of the filing of the claims` IS A DATE
      `the date the trustee or receiver inspected the claims` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 296(a) the claims were inspected within 30 days after the notice` MEANS
    `the date the trustee or receiver inspected the claims` AT MOST (`the date` `s 296(a) the time after the notice to inspect the claims` `after` `the date the trustee or receiver received the Register's notice of the filing of the claims`)

-- "if the trustee or receiver or any creditor shall not be satisfied with the validity or correctness of the same, or any
-- of them, the trustee or receiver shall forthwith notify the creditors whose claims are disputed of such trustee's or
-- receiver's decision."
-- src:1545 | and if the trustee or receiver or any creditor shall not be satisfied with the validity or correctness of the same, or any of them, the trustee or receiver shall forthwith notify the creditors whose claims are disputed of such trustee’s or receiver’s decision. The trustee or receiver shall require all creditors whose claims are disputed to submit themselves to such examination in relation to their claims as the trustee or receiver shall direct, and the creditors shall produce such books and papers relating to their claims as shall be required. The trustee or receiver shall have power to examine, under oath or affirmation, all witnesses produced before such trustee or receiver touching the claims, and shall pass upon and allow or disallow the claims, or any part thereof, and notify the claimants of such trustee’s or receiver’s determination.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 296(a) (src:1545)
GIVEN `the trustee or receiver is not satisfied with the validity or correctness of the claim` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a creditor is not satisfied with the validity or correctness of the claim` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 296(a) the trustee or receiver must forthwith notify the creditor whose claim is disputed of the decision` MEANS
    `the trustee or receiver is not satisfied with the validity or correctness of the claim` OR `a creditor is not satisfied with the validity or correctness of the claim`

-- "The trustee or receiver shall require all creditors whose claims are disputed to submit themselves to such
-- examination in relation to their claims as the trustee or receiver shall direct, and the creditors shall produce such
-- books and papers relating to their claims as shall be required."
-- src:1545 | The trustee or receiver shall require all creditors whose claims are disputed to submit themselves to such examination in relation to their claims as the trustee or receiver shall direct, and the creditors shall produce such books and papers relating to their claims as shall be required. The trustee or receiver shall have power to examine, under oath or affirmation, all witnesses produced before such trustee or receiver touching the claims, and shall pass upon and allow or disallow the claims, or any part thereof, and notify the claimants of such trustee’s or receiver’s determination.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 296(a) (src:1545)
