`s 296(a) the creditor whose claim is disputed must produce the books and papers required` MEANS
    `the creditor’s claim is disputed` AND `the trustee or receiver has required the production of books and papers relating to the claim`

-- "The trustee or receiver shall have power to examine, under oath or affirmation, all witnesses produced before such
-- trustee or receiver touching the claims, and shall pass upon and allow or disallow the claims, or any part thereof, and
-- notify the claimants of such trustee’s or receiver’s determination."
-- src:1545 | The trustee or receiver shall have power to examine, under oath or affirmation, all witnesses produced before such trustee or receiver touching the claims, and shall pass upon and allow or disallow the claims, or any part thereof, and notify the claimants of such trustee’s or receiver’s determination.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 296(a) (src:1545)
DECLARE `s 296(a) Power or duty of the trustee or receiver on the claims` IS ONE OF
    `to examine, under oath or affirmation, all witnesses produced before the trustee or receiver touching the claims`
    `to pass upon and allow or disallow the claims, or any part of them`
    `to notify the claimants of the determination`

-- src:1545 | The trustee or receiver shall have power to examine, under oath or affirmation, all witnesses produced before such trustee or receiver touching the claims, and shall pass upon and allow or disallow the claims, or any part thereof, and notify the claimants of such trustee’s or receiver’s determination.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 296(a) (src:1545)
