    WHEN `to notify the claimants of the determination` THEN TRUE

-- Subsection (b): "Every creditor or claimant who shall have received notice from the receiver or trustee that such
-- creditor’s or claimant’s claim has been disallowed in whole or in part may appeal to the Court of Chancery within 30
-- days thereafter." The 30th day after receiving the notice is the last day.
-- src:1546 | Every creditor or claimant who shall have received notice from the receiver or trustee that such creditor’s or claimant’s claim has been disallowed in whole or in part may appeal to the Court of Chancery within 30 days thereafter. The Court, after hearing, shall determine the rights of the parties.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 296(b) (src:1546)
`s 296(b) the time after the notice of disallowance to appeal` MEANS `period in days` 30

@ref 8 Del. C. § 296(b) (src:1546)
GIVEN `the creditor or claimant received notice from the receiver or trustee that the claim has been disallowed in whole or in part` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the creditor or claimant received the notice` IS A DATE
      `the date the creditor or claimant appeals to the Court of Chancery` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 296(b) the creditor or claimant may appeal to the Court of Chancery` MEANS
        `the creditor or claimant received notice from the receiver or trustee that the claim has been disallowed in whole or in part`
    AND `the date the creditor or claimant appeals to the Court of Chancery` AT MOST (`the date` `s 296(b) the time after the notice of disallowance to appeal` `after` `the date the creditor or claimant received the notice`)

§§ `s 297 Sale of perishable or deteriorating property`

-- "Whenever the property of a corporation is at the time of the appointment of a receiver or trustee encumbered with
-- liens of any character, and the validity, extent or legality of any lien is disputed or brought in question, and the
-- property of the corporation is of a character which will deteriorate in value pending the litigation respecting the lien,
-- the Court of Chancery may order the receiver or trustee to sell the property of the corporation, clear of all
-- encumbrances, at public or private sale, for the best price that can be obtained therefor".
-- src:1550 | Whenever the property of a corporation is at the time of the appointment of a receiver or trustee encumbered with liens of any character, and the validity, extent or legality of any lien is disputed or brought in question, and the property of the corporation is of a character which will deteriorate in value pending the litigation respecting the lien, the Court of Chancery may order the receiver or trustee to sell the property of the corporation, clear of all encumbrances, at public or private sale, for the best price that can be obtained therefor, …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 297 (src:1550)
GIVEN `the property of the corporation is encumbered with liens of any character at the time of the appointment of the receiver or trustee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the validity, extent or legality of a lien is disputed or brought in question` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the property is of a character which will deteriorate in value pending the litigation respecting the lien` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 297 the Court of Chancery may order the receiver or trustee to sell the property clear of all encumbrances` MEANS
        `the property of the corporation is encumbered with liens of any character at the time of the appointment of the receiver or trustee`
    AND `the validity, extent or legality of a lien is disputed or brought in question`
    AND `the property is of a character which will deteriorate in value pending the litigation respecting the lien`

-- "and pay the net proceeds arising from the sale thereof after deducting the costs of the sale into the Court, there to
-- remain subject to the order of the Court, and to be disposed of as the Court shall direct."
-- src:1550 | and pay the net proceeds arising from the sale thereof after deducting the costs of the sale into the Court, there to remain subject to the order of the Court, and to be disposed of as the Court shall direct.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 297 (src:1550)
GIVEN `the price obtained for the property` IS A NUMBER
      `the costs of the sale` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 297 the net proceeds paid into the Court` MEANS
    `the price obtained for the property` MINUS `the costs of the sale`

§§ `s 298 Compensation, costs and expenses of receiver or trustee`

-- "The Court of Chancery, before making distribution of the assets of a corporation among the creditors or stockholders
-- thereof, shall allow a reasonable compensation to the receiver or trustee for such receiver’s or trustee’s services, and
-- the costs and expenses incurred in and about the execution of such receiver’s or trustee’s trust, and the costs of the
-- proceedings in the Court, to be first paid out of the assets." What is "reasonable" is the Court's: the amounts are
-- inputs. If the charges exceed the assets the text does not say what then happens: NOTHING.
-- src:1554 | The Court of Chancery, before making distribution of the assets of a corporation among the creditors or stockholders thereof, shall allow a reasonable compensation to the receiver or trustee for such receiver’s or trustee’s services, and the costs and expenses incurred in and about the execution of such receiver’s or trustee’s trust, and the costs of the proceedings in the Court, to be first paid out of the assets.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 298 (src:1554)
GIVEN `the assets of the corporation` IS A NUMBER
      `the compensation the Court of Chancery allows the receiver or trustee` IS A NUMBER
      `the costs and expenses incurred in and about the execution of the trust` IS A NUMBER
      `the costs of the proceedings in the Court` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 298 the assets left for distribution among the creditors or stockholders` MEANS
    IF `the assets of the corporation` AT LEAST (`the compensation the Court of Chancery allows the receiver or trustee` PLUS `the costs and expenses incurred in and about the execution of the trust` PLUS `the costs of the proceedings in the Court`)
    THEN JUST (`the assets of the corporation` MINUS (`the compensation the Court of Chancery allows the receiver or trustee` PLUS `the costs and expenses incurred in and about the execution of the trust` PLUS `the costs of the proceedings in the Court`))
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 299 Substitution of trustee or receiver as party; abatement of actions`

-- "A trustee or receiver, upon application by such receiver or trustee in the court in which any suit is pending, shall be
-- substituted as party plaintiff in the place of the corporation in any suit or proceeding which was so pending at the time
-- of such receiver’s or trustee’s appointment."
-- src:1558 | A trustee or receiver, upon application by such receiver or trustee in the court in which any suit is pending, shall be substituted as party plaintiff in the place of the corporation in any suit or proceeding which was so pending at the time of such receiver’s or trustee’s appointment. No action against a trustee or receiver of a corporation shall abate by reason of such receiver’s or trustee’s death, but, upon suggestion of the facts on the record, shall be continued against such receiver’s or trustee’s successor or against the corporation in case no new trustee or receiver is appointed.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 299 (src:1558)
GIVEN `the trustee or receiver has applied in the court in which the suit is pending` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation is the plaintiff in the suit or proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the suit or proceeding was pending at the time of the trustee’s or receiver’s appointment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 299 the trustee or receiver is substituted as party plaintiff in the place of the corporation` MEANS
        `the trustee or receiver has applied in the court in which the suit is pending`
    AND `the corporation is the plaintiff in the suit or proceeding`
    AND `the suit or proceeding was pending at the time of the trustee’s or receiver’s appointment`

-- "No action against a trustee or receiver of a corporation shall abate by reason of such receiver’s or trustee’s death, but,
-- upon suggestion of the facts on the record, shall be continued against such receiver’s or trustee’s successor or against
-- the corporation in case no new trustee or receiver is appointed." Without a suggestion of the facts on the record the
-- sentence does not say against whom it continues: NOTHING.
-- src:1558 | No action against a trustee or receiver of a corporation shall abate by reason of such receiver’s or trustee’s death, but, upon suggestion of the facts on the record, shall be continued against such receiver’s or trustee’s successor or against the corporation in case no new trustee or receiver is appointed.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 299 (src:1558)
DECLARE `s 299 Party against whom an action continues` IS ONE OF
    `the successor of the trustee or receiver`
    `the corporation`

-- src:1558 | No action against a trustee or receiver of a corporation shall abate by reason of such receiver’s or trustee’s death, but, upon suggestion of the facts on the record, shall be continued against such receiver’s or trustee’s successor or against the corporation in case no new trustee or receiver is appointed.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 299 (src:1558)
GIVEN `the facts have been suggested on the record` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a new trustee or receiver has been appointed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 299 Party against whom an action continues`
`s 299 the action against the trustee or receiver, who has died, continues against` MEANS
    IF `the facts have been suggested on the record`
    THEN JUST (IF `a new trustee or receiver has been appointed` THEN `the successor of the trustee or receiver` ELSE `the corporation`)
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 300 Employee’s lien for wages when corporation insolvent`

-- "Whenever any corporation of this State, or any foreign corporation doing business in this State, shall become
-- insolvent, the employees doing labor or service of whatever character in the regular employ of the corporation, shall
-- have a lien upon the assets thereof for the amount of the wages due to them, not exceeding 2 months’ wages
-- respectively, which shall be paid prior to any other debt or debts of the corporation. The word “employee” shall not be
-- construed to include any of the officers of the corporation."
-- src:1562 | Whenever any corporation of this State, or any foreign corporation doing business in this State, shall become insolvent, the employees doing labor or service of whatever character in the regular employ of the corporation, shall have a lien upon the assets thereof for the amount of the wages due to them, not exceeding 2 months’ wages respectively, which shall be paid prior to any other debt or debts of the corporation. The word “employee” shall not be construed to include any of the officers of the corporation.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 300 (src:1562)
GIVEN `the corporation is a corporation of this State or a foreign corporation doing business in this State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation has become insolvent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person does labor or service of whatever character in the regular employ of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 300 the person has a lien upon the assets of the corporation for wages, paid prior to any other debt` MEANS
        `the corporation is a corporation of this State or a foreign corporation doing business in this State`
    AND `the corporation has become insolvent`
    AND `the person does labor or service of whatever character in the regular employ of the corporation`
    AND (NOT `the person is an officer of the corporation`)

-- src:1562 | Whenever any corporation of this State, or any foreign corporation doing business in this State, shall become insolvent, the employees doing labor or service of whatever character in the regular employ of the corporation, shall have a lien upon the assets thereof for the amount of the wages due to them, not exceeding 2 months’ wages respectively, which shall be paid prior to any other debt or debts of the corporation. The word “employee” shall not be construed to include any of the officers of the corporation.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 300 (src:1562)
`s 300 the months of wages the lien does not exceed` MEANS 2

@ref 8 Del. C. § 300 (src:1562)
GIVEN `the person has a lien under section 300` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the wages due to the person` IS A NUMBER
      `the person's wages for one month` IS A NUMBER -- the text speaks of "2 months’ wages": a month's wages is the caller's figure
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 300 the amount of the lien for wages` MEANS
    IF `the person has a lien under section 300`
    THEN min `the wages due to the person` (`s 300 the months of wages the lien does not exceed` TIMES `the person's wages for one month`)
    ELSE 0

§§ `s 301 Discontinuance of liquidation`

-- "The liquidation of the assets and business of an insolvent corporation may be discontinued at any time during the
-- liquidation proceedings when it is established that cause for liquidation no longer exists."
-- src:1566 | The liquidation of the assets and business of an insolvent corporation may be discontinued at any time during the liquidation proceedings when it is established that cause for liquidation no longer exists. In such event the Court of Chancery in its discretion, and subject to such condition as it may deem appropriate, may dismiss the proceedings and direct the receiver or trustee to redeliver to the corporation all of its remaining property and assets.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 301 (src:1566)
GIVEN `it is established that cause for liquidation no longer exists` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 301 the liquidation of the assets and business of the insolvent corporation may be discontinued` MEANS
    `it is established that cause for liquidation no longer exists`

-- "In such event the Court of Chancery in its discretion, and subject to such condition as it may deem appropriate, may
-- dismiss the proceedings and direct the receiver or trustee to redeliver to the corporation all of its remaining property
-- and assets." The Court's discretion is a plain input.
-- src:1566 | In such event the Court of Chancery in its discretion, and subject to such condition as it may deem appropriate, may dismiss the proceedings and direct the receiver or trustee to redeliver to the corporation all of its remaining property and assets.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 301 (src:1566)
GIVEN `it is established that cause for liquidation no longer exists` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court of Chancery, in its discretion, dismisses the proceedings and directs the redelivery` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 301 the receiver or trustee must redeliver to the corporation all of its remaining property and assets` MEANS
        `it is established that cause for liquidation no longer exists`
    AND `the Court of Chancery, in its discretion, dismisses the proceedings and directs the redelivery`

§§ `s 302 Compromise or arrangement between corporation and creditors or stockholders`

-- Subsection (a): where the provision permitted by section 102(b)(2) (out of range: piece dg1) is in the original
-- certificate of incorporation, "all persons who become creditors or stockholders thereof shall be deemed to have become
-- such creditors or stockholders subject in all respects to that provision and the same shall be absolutely binding upon
-- them"; where the provision is inserted by an amendment, so are those who "become creditors or stockholders of such
-- corporation after such amendment" (a person who was one before the amendment, or became one on the day of it, is
-- not covered by the text: NOTHING; fork F11). With no such provision the subsection does not speak.
-- src:1570 | (a) Whenever the provision permitted by § 102(b)(2) of this title is included in the original certificate of incorporation of any corporation, all persons who become creditors or stockholders thereof shall be deemed to have become such creditors or stockholders subject in all respects to that provision and the same shall be absolutely binding upon them. Whenever that provision is inserted in the certificate of incorporation of any such corporation by an amendment of its certificate all persons who become creditors or stockholders of such corporation after such amendment shall be deemed to have become such creditors or stockholders subject in all respects to that provision and the same shall be absolutely binding upon them.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 302(a) (src:1570)
GIVEN `the provision permitted by § 102(b)(2) is included in the original certificate of incorporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the provision was inserted in the certificate of incorporation by an amendment, if it was` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date the person became a creditor or stockholder` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 302(a) the person is bound by the provision permitted by section 102(b)(2)` MEANS
    IF `the provision permitted by § 102(b)(2) is included in the original certificate of incorporation`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE (CONSIDER `the date the provision was inserted in the certificate of incorporation by an amendment, if it was`
          WHEN JUST amended THEN (IF `the date the person became a creditor or stockholder` GREATER THAN amended THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING)
          WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING)

-- Subsection (b): the Court of Chancery "may administer and enforce any compromise or arrangement made pursuant to the
-- provision contained in § 102(b)(2) of this title and may restrain, pendente lite, all actions and proceedings against any
-- corporation with respect to which the Court shall have begun the administration and enforcement of that provision and
-- may appoint a temporary receiver for such corporation and may grant the receiver such powers as it deems proper, and
-- may make and enforce such rules as it deems necessary for the exercise of such jurisdiction."
-- src:1571 | (b) The Court of Chancery may administer and enforce any compromise or arrangement made pursuant to the provision contained in § 102(b)(2) of this title and may restrain, pendente lite, all actions and proceedings against any corporation with respect to which the Court shall have begun the administration and enforcement of that provision and may appoint a temporary receiver for such corporation and may grant the receiver such powers as it deems proper, and may make and enforce such rules as it deems necessary for the exercise of such jurisdiction.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 302(b) (src:1571)
DECLARE `s 302(b) Power of the Court of Chancery` IS ONE OF
    `to administer and enforce a compromise or arrangement made pursuant to the provision`
    `to restrain, pendente lite, all actions and proceedings against the corporation`
    `to appoint a temporary receiver for the corporation and grant the receiver such powers as it deems proper`
    `to make and enforce such rules as it deems necessary for the exercise of its jurisdiction`

-- src:1571 | (b) The Court of Chancery may administer and enforce any compromise or arrangement made pursuant to the provision contained in § 102(b)(2) of this title and may restrain, pendente lite, all actions and proceedings against any corporation with respect to which the Court shall have begun the administration and enforcement of that provision and may appoint a temporary receiver for such corporation and may grant the receiver such powers as it deems proper, and may make and enforce such rules as it deems necessary for the exercise of such jurisdiction.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 302(b) (src:1571)
GIVEN `the power` IS A `s 302(b) Power of the Court of Chancery`
      `a compromise or arrangement was made pursuant to the provision contained in § 102(b)(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court of Chancery has begun the administration and enforcement of that provision with respect to the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 302(b) the Court of Chancery has the power` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the power`
    WHEN `to administer and enforce a compromise or arrangement made pursuant to the provision` THEN `a compromise or arrangement was made pursuant to the provision contained in § 102(b)(2)`
    OTHERWISE `the Court of Chancery has begun the administration and enforcement of that provision with respect to the corporation`

§§ `s 303 Proceeding under the Federal Bankruptcy Code of the United States; effectuation`

-- Subsection (a): "Any corporation of this State, an order for relief with respect to which has been entered pursuant to
-- the Federal Bankruptcy Code ... may put into effect and carry out any decrees and orders of the court or judge in such
-- bankruptcy proceeding and may take any corporate action provided or directed by such decrees and orders, without
-- further action by its directors or stockholders." The Federal Bankruptcy Code is not among the inputs: that an order
-- for relief has been entered is a plain input. Subsection (d): the section ceases to apply on the entry of a final decree
-- closing the case and discharging the trustee or trustees.
-- src:1575 | Any corporation of this State, an order for relief with respect to which has been entered pursuant to the Federal Bankruptcy Code, 11 U.S.C. § 101 et seq., or any successor statute, may put into effect and carry out any decrees and orders of the court or judge in such bankruptcy proceeding and may take any corporate action provided or directed by such decrees and orders, without further action by its directors or stockholders. …
-- src:1578 | (d) This section shall cease to apply to such corporation upon the entry of a final decree in the bankruptcy proceeding closing the case and discharging the trustee or trustees, if any; …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 303(a) (src:1575), (d) (src:1578)
GIVEN `the corporation is a corporation of this State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an order for relief with respect to the corporation has been entered pursuant to the Federal Bankruptcy Code` IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: 11 U.S.C. § 101 et seq.
      `the corporate action is provided or directed by a decree or order of the court or judge in the bankruptcy proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a final decree in the bankruptcy proceeding has been entered closing the case and discharging the trustee or trustees, if any` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 303(a) the corporation may take the corporate action without further action by its directors or stockholders` MEANS
        `the corporation is a corporation of this State`
    AND `an order for relief with respect to the corporation has been entered pursuant to the Federal Bankruptcy Code`
    AND `the corporate action is provided or directed by a decree or order of the court or judge in the bankruptcy proceeding`
    AND (NOT `a final decree in the bankruptcy proceeding has been entered closing the case and discharging the trustee or trustees, if any`)

-- "Such power and authority may be exercised, and such corporate action may be taken, as may be directed by such
-- decrees or orders, by the trustee or trustees of such corporation appointed or elected in the bankruptcy proceeding (or a
-- majority thereof), or if none be appointed or elected and acting, by designated officers of the corporation, or by a
-- representative appointed by the court or judge, with like effect as if exercised and taken by unanimous action of the
-- directors and stockholders of the corporation."
-- src:1575 | Such power and authority may be exercised, and such corporate action may be taken, as may be directed by such decrees or orders, by the trustee or trustees of such corporation appointed or elected in the bankruptcy proceeding (or a majority thereof), or if none be appointed or elected and acting, by designated officers of the corporation, or by a representative appointed by the court or judge, with like effect as if exercised and taken by unanimous action of the directors and stockholders of the corporation.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 303(a) (src:1575)
DECLARE `s 303 Person who exercises the corporation’s power` IS ONE OF
    `a majority of the trustees appointed or elected in the bankruptcy proceeding`
    `the designated officers of the corporation`
    `a representative appointed by the court or judge`

-- src:1575 | Such power and authority may be exercised, and such corporate action may be taken, as may be directed by such decrees or orders, by the trustee or trustees of such corporation appointed or elected in the bankruptcy proceeding (or a majority thereof), or if none be appointed or elected and acting, by designated officers of the corporation, or by a representative appointed by the court or judge, with like effect as if exercised and taken by unanimous action of the directors and stockholders of the corporation.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 303(a) (src:1575)
GIVEN `the person` IS A `s 303 Person who exercises the corporation’s power`
      `trustees have been appointed or elected in the bankruptcy proceeding and are acting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 303(a) the person may exercise the corporation’s power and take the corporate action` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the person`
    WHEN `a majority of the trustees appointed or elected in the bankruptcy proceeding` THEN `trustees have been appointed or elected in the bankruptcy proceeding and are acting`
    OTHERWISE NOT `trustees have been appointed or elected in the bankruptcy proceeding and are acting`

-- Subsection (b): the corporation may, in the manner provided in subsection (a), take the actions it lists; "be dissolved,
-- transfer all or part of its assets, merge or consolidate as permitted by this chapter, in which case, however, no
-- stockholder shall have any statutory right of appraisal of such stockholder’s stock"; and "lease its property and
-- franchises to any corporation, if permitted by law".
-- src:1576 | (b) Such corporation may, in the manner provided in subsection (a) of this section, but without limiting the generality or effect of the foregoing, alter, amend or repeal its bylaws; constitute or reconstitute and classify or reclassify its board of directors, and name, constitute or appoint directors and officers in place of or in addition to all or some of the directors or officers then in office; amend its certificate of incorporation, and make any change in its capital or capital stock, or any other amendment, change, or alteration, or provision, authorized by this chapter; be dissolved, transfer all or part of its assets, merge or consolidate as permitted by this chapter, in which case, however, no stockholder shall have any statutory right of appraisal of such stockholder’s stock; change the location of its registered office, change its registered agent, and remove or appoint any agent to receive service of process; authorize and fix the terms, manner and conditions of, the issuance of bonds, debentures or other obligations, whether or not convertible into stock of any class, or bearing warrants or other evidences of optional rights to purchase or subscribe for stock of any class; or lease its property and franchises to any corporation, if permitted by law.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 303(b) (src:1576)
DECLARE `s 303(b) Corporate action` IS ONE OF
    `alter, amend or repeal its bylaws`
    `constitute or reconstitute and classify or reclassify its board of directors, and name, constitute or appoint directors and officers`
    `amend its certificate of incorporation, make any change in its capital or capital stock, or make any other amendment, change, alteration or provision authorized by this chapter`
    `be dissolved`
    `transfer all or part of its assets`
    `merge or consolidate as permitted by this chapter`
    `change the location of its registered office, change its registered agent, and remove or appoint any agent to receive service of process`
    `authorize and fix the terms, manner and conditions of the issuance of bonds, debentures or other obligations, whether or not convertible into stock or bearing warrants or other evidences of optional rights`
    `lease its property and franchises to any corporation`

-- src:1576 | (b) Such corporation may, in the manner provided in subsection (a) of this section, but without limiting the generality or effect of the foregoing, alter, amend or repeal its bylaws; constitute or reconstitute and classify or reclassify its board of directors, and name, constitute or appoint directors and officers in place of or in addition to all or some of the directors or officers then in office; amend its certificate of incorporation, and make any change in its capital or capital stock, or any other amendment, change, or alteration, or provision, authorized by this chapter; be dissolved, transfer all or part of its assets, merge or consolidate as permitted by this chapter, in which case, however, no stockholder shall have any statutory right of appraisal of such stockholder’s stock; change the location of its registered office, change its registered agent, and remove or appoint any agent to receive service of process; authorize and fix the terms, manner and conditions of, the issuance of bonds, debentures or other obligations, whether or not convertible into stock of any class, or bearing warrants or other evidences of optional rights to purchase or subscribe for stock of any class; or lease its property and franchises to any corporation, if permitted by law.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 303(b) (src:1576)
GIVEN `the corporate action` IS A `s 303(b) Corporate action`
      `the corporation may take corporate action in the manner provided in subsection (a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the lease is permitted by law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 303(b) the corporation may take the listed corporate action in the manner provided in subsection (a)` MEANS
        `the corporation may take corporate action in the manner provided in subsection (a)`
    AND (CONSIDER `the corporate action`
         WHEN `lease its property and franchises to any corporation` THEN `the lease is permitted by law`
         OTHERWISE TRUE)

-- A merger or consolidation under subsection (b): "no stockholder shall have any statutory right of appraisal of such
-- stockholder’s stock". For the other listed actions the subsection says nothing of appraisal: NOTHING.
-- src:1576 | be dissolved, transfer all or part of its assets, merge or consolidate as permitted by this chapter, in which case, however, no stockholder shall have any statutory right of appraisal of such stockholder’s stock; …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 303(b) (src:1576)
GIVEN `the corporate action` IS A `s 303(b) Corporate action`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 303(b) a stockholder has a statutory right of appraisal of the stockholder’s stock` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the corporate action`
    WHEN `merge or consolidate as permitted by this chapter` THEN JUST FALSE
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- Subsection (c): "A certificate of any amendment, change or alteration, or of dissolution, or any agreement of merger or
-- consolidation, made by such corporation pursuant to the foregoing provisions, shall be filed with the Secretary of State in
-- accordance with § 103 of this title ... Such certificate, agreement of merger or other instrument shall be made, executed
-- and acknowledged, as may be directed by such decrees or orders, by the trustee or trustees appointed or elected in the
-- bankruptcy proceeding (or a majority thereof), or, if none be appointed or elected and acting, by the officers of the
-- corporation, or by a representative appointed by the court or judge, and shall certify that provision for the making of such
-- certificate, agreement or instrument is contained in a decree or order of a court or judge having jurisdiction".
-- src:1577 | (c) A certificate of any amendment, change or alteration, or of dissolution, or any agreement of merger or consolidation, made by such corporation pursuant to the foregoing provisions, shall be filed with the Secretary of State in accordance with § 103 of this title, and, subject to § 103(d) of this title, shall thereupon become effective in accordance with its terms and the provisions hereof. Such certificate, agreement of merger or other instrument shall be made, executed and acknowledged, as may be directed by such decrees or orders, by the trustee or trustees appointed or elected in the bankruptcy proceeding (or a majority thereof), or, if none be appointed or elected and acting, by the officers of the corporation, or by a representative appointed by the court or judge, and shall certify that provision for the making of such certificate, agreement or instrument is contained in a decree or order of a court or judge having jurisdiction of a proceeding under such Federal Bankruptcy Code or successor statute.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 303(c) (src:1577)
GIVEN `the instrument was filed with the Secretary of State in accordance with § 103` IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: section 103 (piece dg1)
      `the person who made, executed and acknowledged the instrument` IS A `s 303 Person who exercises the corporation’s power`
      `trustees have been appointed or elected in the bankruptcy proceeding and are acting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the instrument certifies that provision for its making is contained in a decree or order of a court or judge having jurisdiction of a proceeding under the Federal Bankruptcy Code` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 303(c) the certificate, agreement or other instrument is in order` MEANS
        `the instrument was filed with the Secretary of State in accordance with § 103`
    AND (`s 303(a) the person may exercise the corporation’s power and take the corporate action` WITH `the person` IS `the person who made, executed and acknowledged the instrument`, `trustees have been appointed or elected in the bankruptcy proceeding and are acting` IS `trustees have been appointed or elected in the bankruptcy proceeding and are acting`)
    AND `the instrument certifies that provision for its making is contained in a decree or order of a court or judge having jurisdiction of a proceeding under the Federal Bankruptcy Code`

-- Subsection (d), second limb: "the closing of a case and discharge of trustee or trustees, if any, will not affect the
-- validity of any act previously performed pursuant to subsections (a) through (c) of this section." The rule has no
-- input about the closing: closing never changes the answer.
-- src:1578 | provided however, that the closing of a case and discharge of trustee or trustees, if any, will not affect the validity of any act previously performed pursuant to subsections (a) through (c) of this section.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 303(d) (src:1578)
GIVEN `the act was performed pursuant to subsections (a) through (c) before the final decree` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 303(d) the act previously performed remains valid` MEANS
    `the act was performed pursuant to subsections (a) through (c) before the final decree`

-- Subsection (e): "On filing any certificate, agreement, report or other paper made or executed pursuant to this section,
-- there shall be paid to the Secretary of State for the use of the State the same fees as are payable by corporations not in
-- bankruptcy upon the filing of like certificates, agreements, reports or other papers." The fees are section 391
-- (out of range: piece dg11).
-- src:1579 | (e) On filing any certificate, agreement, report or other paper made or executed pursuant to this section, there shall be paid to the Secretary of State for the use of the State the same fees as are payable by corporations not in bankruptcy upon the filing of like certificates, agreements, reports or other papers.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 303(e) (src:1579)
GIVEN `the fee payable under § 391 by a corporation not in bankruptcy for the filing of a like paper` IS A NUMBER -- out of range: section 391 (piece dg11)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 303(e) the fee payable to the Secretary of State on filing the paper` MEANS
    `the fee payable under § 391 by a corporation not in bankruptcy for the filing of a like paper`
